{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this production plan — are we maximizing total profit (unit price minus raw material cost, with the operating costs treated as fixed full-capacity charges that do not depend on how much each machine is used)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the optimization objective and the treatment of operating costs, which are presented as a unified policy choice."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are there any demand limits or minimum production requirements for the three products, or can we produce and sell any non-negative quantity of each product as long as the machine capacity constraints are satisfied?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the existence of demand limits or minimum production requirements versus the ability to produce any non-negative quantity."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Since the operating costs are fixed charges paid whenever a machine is used at all, should the model be allowed to leave a machine completely idle (producing nothing on it) in order to avoid paying its fixed charge, or must every machine be used in the plan?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy decision regarding whether machines can be left idle to avoid fixed costs or if they must all be used."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the fixed operating cost of a machine, is the charge triggered by any positive amount of processing time on that machine (i.e., the machine is \"used\" if total assigned time is greater than zero), or is it triggered only when the machine runs at full capacity?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the trigger condition for fixed operating costs, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the user to choose from."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For each product, must the quantity processed on procedure A exactly equal the quantity processed on procedure B (i.e., every unit that goes through A must also go through B, so the two procedures are perfectly balanced per product), or could a unit be processed on one procedure without the other?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the relationship between quantities processed on two procedures, offering a binary choice between perfect balance and independent processing."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "When a product is processed on multiple eligible machines for the same procedure (e.g., Product I on both A1 and A2), is the processing time per unit the same regardless of which machine it is assigned to, so that the total time on a machine is simply the sum of (units assigned to that machine) times (that product's time on that machine)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking whether processing time is uniform across eligible machines for a given product and procedure."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the production quantities allowed to be fractional (continuous), or must each product be produced in whole units only?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice regarding the granularity of production quantities."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a single planning period (one batch of production), or does the plan span multiple periods where production in one period can carry over to the next?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the structure of the planning horizon (single vs. multi-period), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the fixed operating cost, is the charge per machine a single fixed amount paid once if the machine is used at all, or is it a per-unit cost that scales with the number of units processed on that machine?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the nature of the fixed operating cost (lump sum vs. scaling), which constitutes one independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the raw material cost, is it incurred per unit of product produced (i.e., 0.25 yuan per unit of Product I, 0.35 per unit of Product II, 0.50 per unit of Product III), regardless of which machines process it?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the cost structure and its independence from machine selection."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the revenue, is the unit price (1.25 yuan for Product I, 2.00 yuan for Product II, 2.80 yuan for Product III) the selling price per unit of finished product, so that total revenue is the sum of units produced times the unit price for each product?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the revenue calculation method."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the machine capacity constraint, is the effective machine hours (e.g., 6000 for A1, 10000 for A2) the maximum total processing time that can be assigned to that machine across all products, so the sum of (units of each product on that machine) times (that product's processing time on that machine) must be less than or equal to the effective machine hours?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for confirmation of the interpretation of the machine capacity constraint."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product II, which can be processed on A1 or A2 for procedure A but only on B1 for procedure B, is it allowed to split Product II's production across both A1 and A2 (i.e., some units on A1 and some on A2), as long as the total units on A equals the total units on B1?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking whether splitting production across machines A1 and A2 is permitted under specific conditions."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For Product I, which can be processed on A1 or A2 for procedure A and on B1, B2, or B3 for procedure B, is it allowed to split Product I's production across multiple A machines and multiple B machines simultaneously, as long as the total units on A equals the total units on B?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a specific policy decision regarding production splitting constraints."
}

{
