    "For Product III, which can only be processed on A2 for procedure A and on B2 for procedure B, is it allowed to split Product III's production across A2 and B2, or must all of Product III's units be processed on A2 and all on B2 (which is the same thing since there's only one option each)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a policy choice regarding production splitting, presented as a binary option."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the fixed operating cost, if a machine is used for only a tiny amount of processing time (e.g., 0.001 hours), is the full fixed operating cost still incurred, or is there a minimum threshold of usage below which the cost is not triggered?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response contains a single clarification question asking for a specific policy choice regarding cost triggering thresholds."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the profit calculation, is the total profit equal to (total revenue from all products) minus (total raw material cost for all products) minus (sum of fixed operating costs for all machines that are used), with no other costs or constraints?"
